#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ser Anselmo holds the page against the light."
msgstr "Ser Anselmo drži stranicu prema svitlu."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"See the watermark? This paper was made in Fabriano only this year!\""
msgstr "„{crew|Vidiš|Vidiš|Vidite} vodeni znak? Ovi papir je napravljen u Fabrianu tek ove godine!”"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "So it can not be twenty years old. That is our first proof!"
msgstr "Znači da ne more bit star dvadeset godin. To je naš prvi dokaz!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A watermark never lies, captain."
msgstr "Vodeni znak nikad ne laže, {crew|kapetane|kapetanice|kapetani|kapetanice}."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count can forge words, but not the paper of Fabriano!"
msgstr "Grof more krivotvorit riči, ali ne i papir iz Fabriana!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Paper with a Secret"
msgstr "Papir s tajnon"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Find the paper merchant who can read the charter against the light. Proof 1: the watermark of "
"Fabriano."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Nađi|Nađi|Nađite} trgovca papiron ki zna pročitat povelju prema svitlu. Dokaz 1: vodeni znak"
" iz Fabriana."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The paper mills of Fabriano were among the first in Europe. Their papermakers invented the "
"watermark: a picture inside the paper, which shows only against the light."
msgstr ""
"Mlinovi za papir u Fabrianu bili su među prvima u Europi. Njihovi papirari su izmislili vodeni "
"znak: sliku u papiru ka se vidi samo prema svitlu."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The first proof!"
msgstr "Prvi dokaz!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You found Ser Anselmo, and the watermark speaks."
msgstr "{crew|Naša si|Našla si|Našli ste|Našle ste} ser Anselma, i vodeni znak govori."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count's paper is new, not twenty years old."
msgstr "Grofov papir je nov, a ne star dvadeset godin."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Count's seal looks like the seal of the Viceroy."
msgstr "{crew|Kapetane|Kapetanice|Kapetani|Kapetanice}, Grofov pečat izgleda ka potkraljev pečat."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A seal-maker of Ortona carved seals for him, then quit and hid."
msgstr "Jedan pečatar iz Ortone mu je reza pečate, pa je odusta i sakrija se."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Find him! He can tell the judges the truth."
msgstr "{crew|Nađi|Nađi|Nađite} ga! On more sucima reć istinu."

#. a clue; {hallmark} is a noun phrase like 'a patched red sail'
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The seal-maker has {hallmark}."
msgstr "Pečatar ima {hallmark@acc}."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen the seal-maker who hides from the Count?"
msgstr "Jeste li vidili pečatara ki se skriva od Grofa?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He is hiding here, among the craftsmen! But which one is he?"
msgstr "Tu se skriva, među meštrima! Ma koji je od njih?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which one is the seal-maker? Remember what the people told you!"
msgstr "Koji je pečatar? {crew|Siti se|Siti se|Sitite se} ča su {crew|ti|ti|van} ljudi rekli!"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, that is not the seal-maker! Think of everything you heard."
msgstr ""
"Ne, to nije pečatar! {crew|Siti se svega ča si čuja|Siti se svega ča si čula|Sitite se svega ča "
"ste čuli|Sitite se svega ča ste čule}."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"\"Yes, I carved the Count's seal. He said it was for a play!\" Mastro Nunzio gives you the mould."
msgstr ""
"„Da, ja san reza Grofov pečat. Reka je da je za predstavu!” Meštar Nunzio {crew|ti|ti|van} daje "
"kalup."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the mould of the seal to {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Odnesi|Odnesi|Odnesite} kalup pečata {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Look: the name of the King is spelt wrong on it!"
msgstr "{crew|Vidi|Vidi|Vidite}: kraljevo ime je na njemu krivo napisano!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No seal of the Viceroy has such a mistake. That is our second proof!"
msgstr "Nijedan potkraljev pečat nima takve greške. To je naš drugi dokaz!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I will tell the judges everything, captain."
msgstr "Sucima ću sve reć, {crew|kapetane|kapetanice|kapetani|kapetanice}."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "From now on, I carve only honest seals!"
msgstr "Od sad režen samo poštene pečate!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Seal-Maker of Ortona"
msgstr "Pečatar iz Ortone"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Find the seal-maker who quit the Count and hid. Proof 2: the false seal."
msgstr "{crew|Nađi|Nađi|Nađite} pečatara ki je ostavija Grofa i sakrija se. Dokaz 2: lažni pečat."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Ortona keeps the bones of St. Thomas the Apostle. Sailors of Ortona brought them from the Greek "
"island of Chios in 1258."
msgstr ""
"Ortona čuva moći svetog Tome apostola. Mornari iz Ortone su ih 1258. donili s grčkoga otoka Hija."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The second proof!"
msgstr "Drugi dokaz!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You found Mastro Nunzio, and the false seal is in Trani."
msgstr "{crew|Naša si|Našla si|Našli ste|Našle ste} meštra Nunzija, a lažni pečat je u Traniju."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count spelt the name of the King wrong!"
msgstr "Grof je krivo napisa kraljevo ime!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, an old fisherman here remembers the Count from long ago."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Kapetane|Kapetanice|Kapetani|Kapetanice}, jedan stari ribar ovdi se spominje Grofa od davno."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He says the Count was no count at all, but a young copyist: Bepi Sgorbio!"
msgstr "Kaže da Grof uopće ni bija grof, nego mladi prepisivač: Bepi Sgorbio!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bepi lived on the Gargano. Ask about him there."
msgstr "Bepi je živija na Garganu. {crew|Pitaj|Pitaj|Pitajte} za njega tamo."

#. a clue; {fact} is a noun phrase like 'the town with the great Roman arena'
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bepi had a friend in {fact}."
msgstr "Bepi je često iša {fact@to}, k jednon prijatelju."

#. a clue; {fact} is a noun phrase like 'the town with the great Roman arena'
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ask in {fact}. They knew Bepi there."
msgstr "{crew|Idi|Idi|Idite} {fact@to} i {crew|pitaj|pitaj|pitajte}: tamo su poznavali Bepija."

#. a clue; {fact} is a noun phrase like 'the town with the great Roman arena'
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bepi copied letters for the people of {fact}."
msgstr "Bepi je hodija {fact@to} prepisivat pisma za tamošnji puk."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Did you know Bepi Sgorbio, the copyist?"
msgstr "Jeste li poznavali Bepija Sgorbija, prepisivača?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bepi? He hid a box of his old letters in the cave under the white rock of Vieste!"
msgstr "Bepija? Sakrija je škatulu svojih starih pisama u špilju pod bilon stinon u Viesteu!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The cave under the white rock? I know the way, even in a storm!"
msgstr "Špilja pod bilon stinon? Znan put, i po nevremenu!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here is the box. The letters are signed: Bepi Sgorbio, copyist."
msgstr "Evo škatule. Pisma su potpisana: Bepi Sgorbio, prepisivač."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Fetch Bepi's old letters from the white rock."
msgstr "{crew|Pokupi|Pokupi|Pokupite} Bepijeva stara pisma kod bile stine."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring Bepi's letters to {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Odnesi|Odnesi|Odnesite} Bepijeva pisma {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Let me compare them with the Count's charter..."
msgstr "Da ih usporedin s Grofovon poveljon..."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The same hand wrote them both! That is our third proof!"
msgstr "Ista ruka je napisala i jedno i drugo! To je naš treći dokaz!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Three proofs, captain: the paper, the seal and the letters!"
msgstr "Tri dokaza, {crew|kapetane|kapetanice|kapetani|kapetanice}: papir, pečat i pisma!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The \"Count\" is nobody but Bepi Sgorbio."
msgstr "„Grof” nije niko drugi nego Bepi Sgorbio."

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The White Rock"
msgstr "Bila stina"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Storms around the Gargano. Under the white rock of Pizzomunno lie Bepi's old letters. Proof 3."
msgstr "Nevrime oko Gargana. Pod bilon stinon Pizzomunno leže Bepijeva stara pisma. Dokaz 3."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The tall white rock on the beach of Vieste is called Pizzomunno. A legend says it is a young "
"fisherman who turned to stone while he waited for his love Cristalda, whom the mermaids took away."
msgstr ""
"Visoka bila stina na plaži u Viesteu zove se Pizzomunno. Legenda kaže da je to mladi ribar ki se "
"skamenija dok je čeka svoju dragu Cristaldu, ku su odnile sirene."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The third proof!"
msgstr "Treći dokaz!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You braved the storms of the Gargano."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Nisi se pripa|Nisi se pripala|Niste se pripali|Niste se pripale} nevremena oko Gargana."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/21_white_rock/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bepi's old letters show who the Count really is."
msgstr "Bepijeva stara pisma pokazuju ko je zapravo Grof."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Count is furious about the three proofs."
msgstr "{crew|Kapetane|Kapetanice|Kapetani|Kapetanice}, Grof je bisan zbog tri dokaza."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He dares you to a regatta at Barletta: thirteen boats, like the thirteen knights of 1503!"
msgstr ""
"Izaziva {crew|te|te|vas} na regatu u Barleti: trinaest brodica, ka trinaest vitezov iz 1503.!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "If you win, the whole coast will see that his charms are nothing."
msgstr ""
"Ako {crew|pobidiš|pobidiš|pobidite}, cila obala će vidit da njegove amajlije ne vride ništa."

#. what a rival says when he dares the crew to a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Welcome to the Challenge of Barletta, captain!"
msgstr ""
"Dobro {crew|doša|došla|došli|došle} na Izazov iz Barlete, "
"{crew|kapetane|kapetanice|kapetani|kapetanice}!"

#. what a rival says when he dares the crew to a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Thirteen boats, three buoys, and glory for the winner!"
msgstr "Trinaest brodica, tri bove i slava za pobidnika!"

#. what a rival says when he dares the crew to a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "My yellow boat will leave you all behind!"
msgstr "Moja žuta brodica će vas sve ostavit iza sebe!"

#. what a rival says before a rematch of a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ha! Back for another lesson?"
msgstr "Ha! Opet {crew|si tu|si tu|ste tu} po novu lekciju?"

#. what a rival says before a rematch of a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Again: thirteen boats, three buoys!"
msgstr "Opet: trinaest brodica, tri bove!"

#. what the crew hears after winning a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Impossible! I took the short way, and you still won?"
msgstr ""
"Nemoguće! Iša san kraćin putem, a {crew|ti si ipak pobidija|ti si ipak pobidila|vi ste ipak "
"pobidili|vi ste ipak pobidile}?"

#. what the crew hears after winning a race, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The crowd of Barletta cheers for the fair captain!"
msgstr ""
"Puk u Barleti kliče {crew|poštenon kapetanu|poštenoj kapetanici|poštenin kapetanima|poštenin "
"kapetanicama}!"

#. what the crew hears when a rival won the race, one short sentence
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count was back first, but he cheated! The fishermen ask for a rematch tomorrow."
msgstr "Grof se prvi vratija, ali je varaja! Ribari oće novu regatu sutra."

#. what the crew hears when a rival cheats in a race, one short sentence
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count cuts through the shallows and skips a buoy! That's cheating!"
msgstr "Grof siče priko plićine i priskače bovu! To je varanje!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The whole town saw it: the Count cheated, and you won fairly!"
msgstr ""
"Cili grad je vidija: Grof je varaja, a {crew|ti si pošteno pobidija|ti si pošteno pobidila|vi ste "
"pošteno pobidili|vi ste pošteno pobidile}!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I hammered you a horseshoe, for luck."
msgstr "Iskova san {crew|ti|ti|van} potkovu, za sriću."

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Challenge of Barletta"
msgstr "Izazov iz Barlete"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Count dares the crew to a regatta of thirteen boats, as the thirteen knights of 1503. He "
"cheats through the shallows; the crew wins fairly."
msgstr ""
"Grof izaziva posadu na regatu od trinaest brodica, ka trinaest vitezov iz 1503. On vara priko "
"plićine, a posada pobiđuje pošteno."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Challenge of Barletta in 1503 began with an insult at a dinner: a French knight said that the "
"Italians were poor knights. Thirteen knights of each side met in a tournament, and the Italians "
"won."
msgstr ""
"Izazov iz Barlete 1503. počeja je uvridon na večeri: jedan francuski vitez je reka da su Talijani "
"slabi vitezi. Trinaest vitezov sa svake strane srilo se na turniru, i Talijani su pobidili."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A fair win!"
msgstr "Poštena pobida!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count cut through the shallows, and still you won."
msgstr ""
"Grof je prisika priko plićine, a {crew|ti si ipak pobidija|ti si ipak pobidila|vi ste ipak "
"pobidili|vi ste ipak pobidile}."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/22_challenge_of_barletta/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "All of Barletta saw who sails fairly."
msgstr "Cila Barleta je vidila ko jidri pošteno."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain! It's me, Luka, the ship's boy. Remember?"
msgstr ""
"{crew|Kapetane|Kapetanice|Kapetani|Kapetanice}! To san ja, Luka, mali mornar. {crew|Sićaš se|Sićaš"
" se|Sićate se}?"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count bought up all the olive oil, and he sells it at three times the price."
msgstr "Grof je pokupova svo maslinovo ulje, a prodaje ga triput skuplje."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But Vito of Monopoli hid some olives. Help him press them!"
msgstr ""
"Ali Vito iz Monopolija je sakrija malo maslina. {crew|Pomozi|Pomozi|Pomozite} mu napravit ulje!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take this salt along: on this coast, salt buys almost anything."
msgstr "{crew|Uzmi|Uzmi|Uzmite} ovu sol: na ovoj obali za sol se more dobit skoro sve."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "My olives are picked, but the Count's men took my pressing mats."
msgstr "Masline su mi obrane, ma Grofovi ljudi su mi uzeli fiškule za prešu."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Without mats, the press gives no oil. Donata of Brindisi weaves them!"
msgstr "Bez fiškula preša ne da ulja. Donata iz Brindizija ih plete!"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Fine mats! The press is turning..."
msgstr "Lipi fiškuli! Preša se vrti..."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here is the oil, captain. Take it to the market of Bari."
msgstr ""
"Evo ulja, {crew|kapetane|kapetanice|kapetani|kapetanice}. {crew|Odnesi|Odnesi|Odnesite} ga na "
"pazar u Bari."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I weave pressing mats from rushes."
msgstr "Ja pletem fiškule od site."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But I need salt for my fish. Do you have salt?"
msgstr "Ma triba mi sol za ribu. {crew|Imaš|Imaš|Imate} li soli?"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/23_oil_for_monopoli/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Salt! Now my fish keeps all winter."
msgstr "Sol! Sad će mi riba trajat cilu zimu."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
